  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The displacement of a particle is $x=t^3-9t$ cm, where $t$ is time in seconds.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the velocity of the particle at 3 s.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$18\\text{ cm/s}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\dot{x}(t)&=3t^2-9\\\\\\dot{x}(3)&=3(3)^2-9\\\\&=18\\text{ cm/s}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the acceleration at 2 s.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$12\\text{ cm/s}^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\dot{x}(t)&=3t^2-9\\\\\\ddot{x}(t)&=6t\\\\\\ddot{x}(2)&=6(2)\\\\&=12\\text{ cm/s}^2\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Show that the particle is initially at the origin, and find any other times that the particle will be at the origin.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(0)=0$; the particle is at the origin again at $t=3\\text{ s}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x(0)&=0^3-9(0)\\\\&=0\\text{ cm}\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe particle is initially at the origin. At the origin, $x=0$:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t^3-9t&=0\\\\t(t^2-9)&=0\\\\t(t-3)(t+3)&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThus $t=-3,0,3$. Since elapsed time satisfies $t\\geq0$, the other time is $t=3\\text{ s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "At what time will the acceleration be $30\\text{ cm s}^{-2}$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=5\\text{ s}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\ddot{x}(t)&=6t\\\\6t&=30\\\\t&=5\\text{ s}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      }
    ]
  },
